  "title": "[dynamo] sys.setrecursionlimit doesn't seem to do anything",
  "issue_id": "167789",
  "bug_description": "```python\nimport sys\nimport torch\n\ndef fn(x, n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return x\n    return fn(x, n - 1) + 1\n\n@torch.compile(backend=\"eager\")\ndef outer(x):\n    return fn(x, 1000)\n\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10000000)\nouter(torch.ones(3))\n```\n\nThis code gives RecursionError even though the recursionlimit was set to a very high value. If we don't compile, then we don't hit a recursion limit. \n\nIf we set `tstate->c_recursion_remaining` to a high value as well somewhere in C dynamo, then we run successfully. So we should add some kind of eval_frame API to modify the C recursion limit.\n\ncc @ezyang @gchanan @kadeng @msaroufim @chauhang @penguinwu @voznesenskym @EikanWang @jgong5 @Guobing-Chen @XiaobingSuper @zhuhaozhe @blzheng @wenzhe-nrv @jiayisunx @chenyang78 @amjames @Lucaskabela",
